LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 4)
# ===================================================================
# 1. INITIALIZATION
# ===================================================================
clear
units           metal
dimension       3
boundary        p f p
atom_style      atomic

# ===================================================================
# 2. ATOM DEFINITION
# ===================================================================
read_data       GaN_ortho.lmp
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (31.89 27.61755 51.85)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  4000 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.008 seconds
change_box      all y delta 0 10
Changing box ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (31.89 37.61755 51.85)

# ===================================================================
# 3. SETTINGS
# ===================================================================
# Define atomic masses (often included in the data file)
mass            1 69.723  # Ga
mass            2 14.007  # N

# Interatomic Potential Setup
# You must download 'library.meam' and the parameter file (e.g., 'GaN.meam')
# from the NIST repository into your working directory.
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * library.meam Ga N GaN.meam Ga N

# Neighbor list parameters
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1 check yes

# ===================================================================
# 4. MINIMIZATION
# ===================================================================
thermo          100
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal temp lx ly lz press

min_style       cg
minimize        1.0e-8 1.0e-8 10000 10000
Neighbor list info ...
  update: every = 1 steps, delay = 0 steps, check = yes
  max neighbors/atom: 2000, page size: 100000
  master list distance cutoff = 6
  ghost atom cutoff = 6
  binsize = 3, bins = 11 13 18
  2 neighbor lists, perpetual/occasional/extra = 2 0 0
  (1) pair meam, perpetual
      attributes: full, newton on
      pair build: full/bin/atomonly
      stencil: full/bin/3d
      bin: standard
  (2) pair meam, perpetual, half/full from (1)
      attributes: half, newton on
      pair build: halffull/newton
      stencil: none
      bin: none
